  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">El Kassib</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADMC Group is a Dutch company active in the healthcare sector. ADMC Group outsources the production of medical equipment and other materials in Egypt. During this process and during the operations of ADMC Group in the healthcare centers, large amounts of waste is produced.Unfortunately, children are involved in collecting, sorting and recycling the waste. This work is classified as hazardous; children are exposed to toxic residues in the waste, have to carry heavy loads and handle dangerous machines for the recycling process. In the &apos;El Kassib&apos; project, multiple stakeholders work together towards the eradication of child labour in the waste management part of their supply chain. The project takes place in El Zabaleen in Cairo, Egypt.&apos;El Kassib&apos; refers to the young man or woman who knows how to make money in the most efficient way. Many children in Egypt dream of being a Kassib.The project&apos;s targets are:&#x2022;	1,382 children (922 boys and 460 girls) working in the waste sector; and&#x2022;	Families of the children working in the waste sector.The project interventions consist of:1.	Awareness sessions on the prevalence and risks of child labour at the national, community and household level;2.	Removing children from labour and providing physical and mental support to the children;3.	Enrolling children in formal education and vocational training;4.	Strengthening the educational institutions through Training-of-Teachers, curriculum development and certification of teachers through the &quot;Champions of Change&quot; programme;5.	Providing trolleys to the workers that can carry the waste;6.	Improving health &amp; safety standards at the local workshops;7.	Training families, the mothers in specific, to generate additional income through textile recycling; and8.	Setting up Village Savings and Loan Associations (VSLAs).</narrative>
  </description>
